Factor out $-1/2$ and use the method of <completing the square> inside the bracket:
$$
-\frac{x^2}{2}+x=-\frac12(x^2-2x)
=\boxed{\frac12-\frac12(x-1)^2}.
$$

= b
{parent=2}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Since $x^2-1=(x-1)(x+1)$, write the <partial fraction decomposition> as $A/(x-1)+B/(x+1)$. Matching the numerator gives $A+B=1$ and $A-B=2$, hence
$$
\boxed{\frac{x+2}{x^2-1}=\frac{3}{2(x-1)}-\frac{1}{2(x+1)},\qquad x\ne\pm1.}
$$

