= Solution
{parent=b}

For $u>0$, the principal <inverse tangent> satisfies $\arctan u+\arctan(1/u)=\pi/2$: the two positive acute angles are complementary. Taking $u=\pi/4$ therefore makes the argument of the <natural logarithm> equal to $(2/\pi)(\pi/2)=1$. The requested value is **$\ln1=0$**.

= 4
{parent=Paper 1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=4}

In one period, <sine> equals $-\sqrt3/2$ at $4\pi/3$ and $5\pi/3$, and lies below that value between them. Since <sine> is a <periodic function> with period $2\pi$, all solutions are:
$$
\boxed{x\in\bigcup_{k\in\mathbb Z}\left[\frac{4\pi}{3}+2\pi k,\ \frac{5\pi}{3}+2\pi k\right].}
$$
The endpoints are included because the inequality is non-strict.

